  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">FCDO: UK-Ukraine university twinning initiative</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">There are eight primary objectives for the scheme in 2023 - 2024: 
1. Initiated partnerships will be supported to transition to full MoU stage, giving 100 full UK-Ukraine twinning partnerships. 
2. Each institutional partnership will deliver a bespoke long-term (3-5 year) programme of activities to support the long-term health of Ukraine&#x2019;s higher education community. 
3. Strategic priorities of the Ukrainian government and higher education community will be identified in partnership, with bespoke, targeted programmes of work established. 
4. Forums for UK and Ukraine institutions will be convened to allow for the regular exchange of insights, experience and good practice, with at least three meetings per year. 
5. A programme of communications and engagement to both promote the impact of the impact of the scheme and UK government funding, and to attract non-UK institutions to engage with the scheme. 
6. Bids for long-term funding to support the strategic priorities of the twinning programme will be developed, with an ambition to leverage &#xA3;5m in additional funding. 
7. Contract management and associated governance and reporting.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">There are five primary objectives for the scheme in 2024 - 2025: 
1. All twins will be supported to developed 3-5 year plans where possible with the aim of ensuring that twins are able to move to sustainable BAU relationships after the end of funding period.
2. Forums for UK and Ukraine institutions will be convened to allow for the regular exchange of insights, experience and good practice, with at least three meetings per year.
3. A programme of communications and engagement to support the sustainability of the scheme, and promote the impact and reputation of the scheme and UK government funding. 
4. Facilitating opportunities for government and stakeholder engagement to support the long term sustainability of the twinning programme.
5. Contract management, associated governance and reporting, risk management and development of exit strategy.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="4" type="70">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Cormack Consultancy Group. Cormack Consultancy Group is the consultancy service in higher education sector, the main sphere of activity is internationalization. CCG operates since 1999 and has established over 900 partnerships all over the world, develops international strategies, helps to establish TNE cooperation and provides other services on the institutional and state level.</narrative>
  </participating-org>
  <participating-org role="1" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UK Foreign Commonwealth and Development Office (FCDO)</narrative>
  </participating-org>
  <participating-org role="4" type="15">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Universities UK. Universities UK International (UUKi) represents the interests of all UK higher education institutions internationally and promotes UK higher education overseas.  It carries out research, analysis and policy development on international higher education and provide advice and guidance to members.</narrative>
  </participating-org>
